#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1368 expect=skipped domain=SM
#note "THE SMSTDTC ALL-FACET GATE (Fix #331 bucket 2, M2-D24 / M3-D18; pin owed by review S9 and authored by Fix #340). The SM dataset deliberately declares no SMSTDTC column, so Requirements.Variables.All [SMSTDTC] rejects the dataset and the rule is SKIPPED naming SMSTDTC. Remove the All entry and the rule EXECUTES: since Fix #330 retired the injected var_exists guard, a bare empty(SMSTDTC) is TRUE on every row of an absent column (absent = all-missing) and nothing else in the Check restricts the rows, so it would fire on EVERY row -- the flood the gate exists for. If this scenario EXECUTES (violation or silent pass), the gate has been removed -- escalate, do not rewrite the pin."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset SM class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Disease Milestones"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SMSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col MIDS     type=Char label="Disease Milestone Instance Name"
col MIDSTYPE type=Char label="Disease Milestone Type"
---
S1 | SM | 001 | 1 | DIAGNOSIS1 | DIAGNOSIS
S1 | SM | 001 | 2 | RELAPSE1 | RELAPSE
